module

public import Mathlib.RingTheory.FiniteType
public import Mathlib.RingTheory.Ideal.Quotient.Operations
public import Mathlib.RingTheory.KrullDimension.Field
public import Mathlib.RingTheory.KrullDimension.NonZeroDivisors
public import Mathlib.RingTheory.KrullDimension.Polynomial
public import Mathlib.RingTheory.Localization.Away.Basic
public import Mathlib.RingTheory.Nilpotent.Lemmas
public import Mathlib.RingTheory.Polynomial.Quotient

/-!
# The thickened origins refuting the equality clause of Stacks 0DS4

Stacks 0DS4 asserts, for a 1-morphism `f : 𝒯 ⟶ 𝒳` locally of finite type of Jacobson,
pseudo-catenary, locally Noetherian algebraic stacks with `|𝒯|` irreducible and `𝒳`
quasi-separated, that `dim(𝒯) ≤ dim(𝒵) + dim_t(𝒯_{f(t)})` with *equality* on a dense open subset,
`𝒵` being the scheme theoretic image of Stacks 0CMI. The inequality clause is true as stated. The
equality clause is **false** as stated: it needs `f` quasi-compact, which the source does not
list. This file is the ring theory of the witness, at the level of the rings of its charts.

The witness is the affine line with infinitely many origins, the `n`-th origin thickened to order
`n`. Put `A n = k[x][ε]/(ε ^ (n + 1), x * ε)` for a field `k` and let `T` be glued out of the
`Spec (A n)` along the identical opens `{x ≠ 0}`; the sections `ε ∈ A n` agree there, so they glue
to a global section `s`, and `t ↦ s` is a morphism `f : T ⟶ 𝔸¹ = Spec k[t]` locally of finite
type. Every hypothesis the source lists holds for `f`, and `f` is not quasi-compact. Now `s` is
nilpotent at each origin, of **unbounded** order: `P(s) = 0` forces `t ^ (n + 1) ∣ P` for every
`n`, so the scheme theoretic image of `f` is all of `𝔸¹` and `dim(𝒵) = 1`, while the set theoretic
image is the single point `t = 0` and the fibre there is `T` with its reduced structure, of
dimension `1`. The equality clause therefore asserts `1 = 1 + 1`.

Shrinking `T` to one chart restores the equality, and does so precisely *by changing `𝒵`*: on
`Spec (A n)` the kernel of `k[t] ⟶ A n` is `(t ^ (n + 1))`, whose scheme theoretic image has
dimension `0`, and `1 = 0 + 1` holds. That is why the shrinking step of the source's own proof
does not prove the stated form, and by Stacks 0CML quasi-compactness of `f` is exactly what makes
`𝒵` the closure of the image of `|f|`.

## Main definitions

* `AlgebraicGeometry.ThickenedOrigin.chartIdeal`: the ideal `(ε ^ (n + 1), x * ε)` of `k[x][ε]`,
  whose quotient is the ring `A n` of the `n`-th chart.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.ThickenedOrigin.epsilon` and `AlgebraicGeometry.ThickenedOrigin.xCoord`: the
  images of `ε` and of `x` in `A n`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.ThickenedOrigin.chartHom`: the chart `k[t] ⟶ A n` of `f`, sending `t` to `ε`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.ThickenedOrigin.reduction`: the reduction `A n ⟶ k[x]`, sending `ε` to `0`;
  it also cuts out the fibre of `f` over `t = 0`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.ThickenedOrigin.truncation`: the auxiliary `A n ⟶ k[t]/(t ^ (n + 1))` sending
  `x` to `0` and `ε` to `t`, which is what sees that `ε` is nilpotent of order exactly `n + 1`.

## Main results

* `AlgebraicGeometry.ThickenedOrigin.nilradical_eq_span_epsilon`,
  `AlgebraicGeometry.ThickenedOrigin.quotientSpanEpsilonEquiv` and
  `AlgebraicGeometry.ThickenedOrigin.awayEquiv`: the nilradical of `A n` is `(ε)`,
  `A n / (ε) ≅ k[x]` and `A n [1/x] ≅ k[x][1/x]` — the last being what makes the glueing of the
  charts of `T` along `{x ≠ 0}` a glueing of identical opens. `A n` is Noetherian by Mathlib's
  instances `Ideal.Quotient.isNoetherianRing` and `Polynomial.isNoetherianRing`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.ThickenedOrigin.epsilon_pow_succ_eq_zero` and
  `AlgebraicGeometry.ThickenedOrigin.epsilon_pow_ne_zero`: `ε` is nilpotent of order exactly
  `n + 1` in `A n`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.ThickenedOrigin.ker_chartHom`: the kernel of the `n`-th chart of `f` is
  `(t ^ (n + 1))`; `AlgebraicGeometry.ThickenedOrigin.ker_chartHom_lt`: these kernels strictly
  decrease, which is the ring theoretic trace of the failure of quasi-compactness.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.ThickenedOrigin.eq_zero_of_forall_chartHom_eq_zero` and
  `AlgebraicGeometry.ThickenedOrigin.iInf_ker_chartHom`: a `P` with `P(s) = 0` is `0`, so the
  scheme theoretic image of `f` is all of `𝔸¹`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.ThickenedOrigin.finiteType_chartHom`: `A n` is generated by `x` over `k[t]`,
  so `f` is locally of finite type.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.ThickenedOrigin.ringKrullDim_quotient_chartIdeal_ne_add`: **the refutation.**
  The dimension of a chart of `T` is not the dimension of the scheme theoretic image of `f` plus
  the dimension of the fibre of `f` through that chart — it is `1`, and they are `1` and `1`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.ThickenedOrigin.ringKrullDim_quotient_chartIdeal_eq_add_ker_chartHom`: the
  contrast. With `𝒵` replaced by the scheme theoretic image of the restriction of `f` to the
  quasi-compact open `Spec (A n)`, the formula does hold: `1 = 0 + 1`.

## Implementation notes

This file is the level of the **rings of the charts**. The glued scheme `T` and the morphism `f`
are built on top of it in `StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/Stacks/ThickenedOriginsScheme.lean`, and
the refutation at the level of algebraic stacks is
`AlgebraicGeometry.Stack.not_forall_dimension_le_add_and_exists_isOpen_dense_eq` in
`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/Stacks/DimensionSchemeTheoreticImageRefutation.lean`. Every
quantity the equality clause of Stacks 0DS4 compares is computed here as the Krull dimension of
an explicit ring:

* `dim(T)`, as the dimension of each of its charts, `ringKrullDim (k[x][ε] ⧸ chartIdeal k n) = 1`
  (`T` is covered by these charts, so this is where its dimension is);
* `dim(𝒵)`, as `ringKrullDim (k[t] ⧸ ⨅ n, ker (chartHom k n)) = 1`, the intersection of the
  kernels of the charts of `f` being the ideal cutting out the scheme theoretic image;
* `dim_t(T_{f(t)})` at the only point of the set theoretic image, as
  `ringKrullDim (A n ⧸ (ε)) = 1`, the fibre ring over `t = 0` being `A n ⊗_{k[t]} k[t]/(t)`,
  which is `A n / (ε)`.

The three homomorphisms out of `A n` are what the proofs run on.
`AlgebraicGeometry.ThickenedOrigin.truncation` kills `x`, so it survives the relation `x * ε = 0`
and detects `ε ^ n ≠ 0`; `AlgebraicGeometry.ThickenedOrigin.reduction` kills `ε` and identifies
the fibre; and the inclusion `AlgebraicGeometry.ThickenedOrigin.xHom` of the coefficient ring is
injective, which is what makes `A n [1/x]` a localization of `k[x]` rather than of a proper
quotient of it.

The results of the `Localization` and `FiniteType` sections are stated for an arbitrary
`k[x]`- resp. `k[t]`-algebra structure whose structure map is the intended one, since `A n` and
`A n [1/x]` already carry other algebra structures over those rings; the instantiations at the
intended structure are `AlgebraicGeometry.ThickenedOrigin.awayEquiv` and
`AlgebraicGeometry.ThickenedOrigin.finiteType_toAlgebra_chartHom`.

This file deliberately carries no `@[stacks]` attribute: it refutes a clause of a tag rather than
formalizing one. The corrected statement of Stacks 0DS4, with `f` quasi-compact, is in
`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/Stacks/DimensionSchemeTheoreticImage.lean`, whose
implementation notes state this counterexample in prose.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0CMI](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0CMI)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0CML](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0CML)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0DS4](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0DS4)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open Polynomial

namespace AlgebraicGeometry.ThickenedOrigin

universe u

variable (k : Type u) [Field k]

/-- The ideal `(ε ^ (n + 1), x * ε)` of `k[x][ε]`. -/
def chartIdeal (n : ℕ) : Ideal (Polynomial (Polynomial k)) :=
  Ideal.span {(X : Polynomial (Polynomial k)) ^ (n + 1), C (X : Polynomial k) * X}

theorem X_pow_succ_mem_chartIdeal (n : ℕ) :
    (X : Polynomial (Polynomial k)) ^ (n + 1) ∈ chartIdeal k n :=
  Ideal.subset_span (Set.mem_insert _ _)

theorem C_X_mul_X_mem_chartIdeal (n : ℕ) :
    C (X : Polynomial k) * X ∈ chartIdeal k n :=
  Ideal.subset_span (Set.mem_insert_of_mem _ rfl)

theorem chartIdeal_le_span_X (n : ℕ) :
    chartIdeal k n ≤ Ideal.span {(X : Polynomial (Polynomial k))} := by
  rw [chartIdeal, Ideal.span_le]
  intro a ha
  simp only [Set.mem_insert_iff, Set.mem_singleton_iff] at ha
  rcases ha with rfl | rfl
  · exact Ideal.mem_span_singleton.2 ⟨X ^ n, by ring⟩
  · exact Ideal.mem_span_singleton.2 ⟨C X, by ring⟩

/-- `k[x][ε] →+* k[t]/(t ^ (n + 1))`, sending `x` to `0` and `ε` to `t`. -/
def truncationAux (n : ℕ) :
    Polynomial (Polynomial k) →+* Polynomial k ⧸ Ideal.span {(X : Polynomial k) ^ (n + 1)} :=
  eval₂RingHom
    (((Ideal.Quotient.mk (Ideal.span {(X : Polynomial k) ^ (n + 1)})).comp C).comp
      (evalRingHom (0 : k)))
    (Ideal.Quotient.mk _ X)

@[simp]
theorem truncationAux_X (n : ℕ) :
    truncationAux k n X = Ideal.Quotient.mk (Ideal.span {(X : Polynomial k) ^ (n + 1)}) X := by
  simp [truncationAux, coe_eval₂RingHom]

@[simp]
theorem truncationAux_C (n : ℕ) (a : Polynomial k) :
    truncationAux k n (C a) =
      Ideal.Quotient.mk (Ideal.span {(X : Polynomial k) ^ (n + 1)}) (C (a.eval 0)) := by
  simp [truncationAux, coe_eval₂RingHom]

theorem truncationAux_eq_zero_of_mem_chartIdeal (n : ℕ) (a : Polynomial (Polynomial k))
    (ha : a ∈ chartIdeal k n) : truncationAux k n a = 0 := by
  have h : chartIdeal k n ≤ RingHom.ker (truncationAux k n) := by
    rw [chartIdeal, Ideal.span_le]
    intro b hb
    simp only [Set.mem_insert_iff, Set.mem_singleton_iff] at hb
    rcases hb with rfl | rfl
    · rw [SetLike.mem_coe, RingHom.mem_ker, map_pow, truncationAux_X, ← map_pow,
        Ideal.Quotient.eq_zero_iff_mem]
      exact Ideal.mem_span_singleton_self _
    · rw [SetLike.mem_coe, RingHom.mem_ker, map_mul, truncationAux_C, truncationAux_X]
      simp
  exact h ha

/-- The truncation `A n →+* k[t]/(t ^ (n + 1))` induced by `x ↦ 0`, `ε ↦ t`. -/
def truncation (n : ℕ) :
    (Polynomial (Polynomial k) ⧸ chartIdeal k n) →+*
      Polynomial k ⧸ Ideal.span {(X : Polynomial k) ^ (n + 1)} :=
  Ideal.Quotient.lift _ (truncationAux k n) (truncationAux_eq_zero_of_mem_chartIdeal k n)

/-- The image of `ε` in `A n`. -/
def epsilon (n : ℕ) : Polynomial (Polynomial k) ⧸ chartIdeal k n :=
  Ideal.Quotient.mk _ X

/-- The image of `x` in `A n`. -/
def xCoord (n : ℕ) : Polynomial (Polynomial k) ⧸ chartIdeal k n :=
  Ideal.Quotient.mk _ (C X)

@[simp]
theorem truncation_epsilon (n : ℕ) :
    truncation k n (epsilon k n) = Ideal.Quotient.mk _ X := by
  rw [epsilon, truncation, Ideal.Quotient.lift_mk, truncationAux_X]

theorem epsilon_pow_succ_eq_zero (n : ℕ) : epsilon k n ^ (n + 1) = 0 := by
  rw [epsilon, ← map_pow, Ideal.Quotient.eq_zero_iff_mem]
  exact X_pow_succ_mem_chartIdeal k n

theorem epsilon_pow_ne_zero (n : ℕ) : epsilon k n ^ n ≠ 0 := by
  intro h
  have h' := congrArg (truncation k n) h
  rw [map_pow, truncation_epsilon, map_zero, ← map_pow, Ideal.Quotient.eq_zero_iff_mem,
    Ideal.mem_span_singleton] at h'
  have := (pow_dvd_pow_iff X_ne_zero not_isUnit_X).1 h'
  omega

instance (n : ℕ) : Nontrivial (Polynomial (Polynomial k) ⧸ chartIdeal k n) := by
  by_contra h
  rw [not_nontrivial_iff_subsingleton] at h
  exact epsilon_pow_ne_zero k n (Subsingleton.elim _ _)

theorem eval_zero_eq_zero_of_mem_chartIdeal (n : ℕ) (a : Polynomial (Polynomial k))
    (ha : a ∈ chartIdeal k n) : evalRingHom (0 : Polynomial k) a = 0 := by
  have h := chartIdeal_le_span_X k n ha
  rw [Ideal.mem_span_singleton, X_dvd_iff, coeff_zero_eq_eval_zero] at h
  exact h

/-- The reduction `A n →+* k[x]`, sending `ε` to `0`. -/
def reduction (n : ℕ) : (Polynomial (Polynomial k) ⧸ chartIdeal k n) →+* Polynomial k :=
  Ideal.Quotient.lift _ (evalRingHom (0 : Polynomial k)) (eval_zero_eq_zero_of_mem_chartIdeal k n)

@[simp]
theorem reduction_mk (n : ℕ) (p : Polynomial (Polynomial k)) :
    reduction k n (Ideal.Quotient.mk _ p) = p.eval 0 := rfl

theorem reduction_surjective (n : ℕ) : Function.Surjective (reduction k n) := fun p =>
  ⟨Ideal.Quotient.mk _ (C p), by simp⟩

theorem reduction_epsilon (n : ℕ) : reduction k n (epsilon k n) = 0 := by
  rw [epsilon, reduction_mk, eval_X]

theorem reduction_xCoord (n : ℕ) : reduction k n (xCoord k n) = X := by
  rw [xCoord, reduction_mk, eval_C]

theorem mk_mem_span_epsilon_iff (n : ℕ) (p : Polynomial (Polynomial k)) :
    Ideal.Quotient.mk (chartIdeal k n) p ∈ Ideal.span {epsilon k n} ↔
      (X : Polynomial (Polynomial k)) ∣ p := by
  constructor
  · intro h
    obtain ⟨q, hq⟩ := Ideal.mem_span_singleton.1 h
    obtain ⟨q', rfl⟩ := Ideal.Quotient.mk_surjective q
    rw [epsilon, ← map_mul, ← sub_eq_zero, ← map_sub, Ideal.Quotient.eq_zero_iff_mem] at hq
    have hdvd := Ideal.mem_span_singleton.1 (chartIdeal_le_span_X k n hq)
    have h2 : (X : Polynomial (Polynomial k)) ∣ X * q' := Dvd.intro _ rfl
    simpa using dvd_add hdvd h2
  · rintro ⟨q, rfl⟩
    exact Ideal.mem_span_singleton.2 ⟨Ideal.Quotient.mk _ q, by rw [epsilon, ← map_mul]⟩

/-- **The kernel of the reduction is the ideal generated by `ε`.** -/
theorem ker_reduction (n : ℕ) : RingHom.ker (reduction k n) = Ideal.span {epsilon k n} := by
  refine Ideal.ext fun a => ?_
  obtain ⟨p, rfl⟩ := Ideal.Quotient.mk_surjective a
  rw [RingHom.mem_ker, mk_mem_span_epsilon_iff, reduction_mk, X_dvd_iff, coeff_zero_eq_eval_zero]

/-- **The nilradical of `A n` is the ideal generated by `ε`.** -/
theorem nilradical_eq_span_epsilon (n : ℕ) :
    nilradical (Polynomial (Polynomial k) ⧸ chartIdeal k n) = Ideal.span {epsilon k n} := by
  refine Ideal.ext fun a => ?_
  obtain ⟨p, rfl⟩ := Ideal.Quotient.mk_surjective a
  rw [mem_nilradical, mk_mem_span_epsilon_iff]
  constructor
  · rintro ⟨m, hm⟩
    rw [← map_pow, Ideal.Quotient.eq_zero_iff_mem] at hm
    have h1 := Ideal.mem_span_singleton.1 (chartIdeal_le_span_X k n hm)
    rw [X_dvd_iff, coeff_zero_eq_eval_zero, eval_pow] at h1
    rw [X_dvd_iff, coeff_zero_eq_eval_zero]
    exact IsNilpotent.eq_zero ⟨m, h1⟩
  · rintro ⟨q, rfl⟩
    refine ⟨n + 1, ?_⟩
    rw [← map_pow, Ideal.Quotient.eq_zero_iff_mem, mul_pow]
    exact Ideal.mul_mem_right _ _ (X_pow_succ_mem_chartIdeal k n)

/-- **`A n / (ε) ≅ k[x]`.** -/
def quotientSpanEpsilonEquiv (n : ℕ) :
    ((Polynomial (Polynomial k) ⧸ chartIdeal k n) ⧸ Ideal.span {epsilon k n}) ≃+* Polynomial k :=
  (Ideal.quotEquivOfEq (ker_reduction k n).symm).trans
    (RingHom.quotientKerEquivOfSurjective (reduction_surjective k n))

/-- The chart of `f : T ⟶ 𝔸¹` over `Spec (A n)`: the map `k[t] →+* A n` sending `t` to `ε`. -/
def chartHom (n : ℕ) : Polynomial k →+* Polynomial (Polynomial k) ⧸ chartIdeal k n :=
  eval₂RingHom
    ((Ideal.Quotient.mk (chartIdeal k n)).comp
      ((C : Polynomial k →+* Polynomial (Polynomial k)).comp (C : k →+* Polynomial k)))
    (epsilon k n)

@[simp]
theorem chartHom_X (n : ℕ) : chartHom k n X = epsilon k n := by
  simp [chartHom, coe_eval₂RingHom]

@[simp]
theorem chartHom_C (n : ℕ) (a : k) :
    chartHom k n (C a) = Ideal.Quotient.mk (chartIdeal k n) (C (C a)) := by
  simp [chartHom, coe_eval₂RingHom]

theorem truncation_comp_chartHom (n : ℕ) :
    (truncation k n).comp (chartHom k n) =
      Ideal.Quotient.mk (Ideal.span {(X : Polynomial k) ^ (n + 1)}) := by
  refine Polynomial.ringHom_ext (fun a => ?_) ?_
  · rw [RingHom.comp_apply, chartHom_C, truncation, Ideal.Quotient.lift_mk, truncationAux_C,
      eval_C]
  · rw [RingHom.comp_apply, chartHom_X, truncation_epsilon]

/-- **The kernel of the `n`-th chart of `f` is `(t ^ (n + 1))`:** a polynomial `P` with
`P(ε) = 0` in `A n` is divisible by `t ^ (n + 1)`. -/
theorem ker_chartHom (n : ℕ) :
    RingHom.ker (chartHom k n) = Ideal.span {(X : Polynomial k) ^ (n + 1)} := by
  refine le_antisymm (fun p hp => ?_) ?_
  · rw [RingHom.mem_ker] at hp
    have h := congrArg (truncation k n) hp
    rw [← RingHom.comp_apply, truncation_comp_chartHom, map_zero,
      Ideal.Quotient.eq_zero_iff_mem] at h
    exact h
  · rw [Ideal.span_le, Set.singleton_subset_iff, SetLike.mem_coe, RingHom.mem_ker, map_pow,
      chartHom_X]
    exact epsilon_pow_succ_eq_zero k n

theorem chartHom_eq_zero_iff (n : ℕ) (p : Polynomial k) :
    chartHom k n p = 0 ↔ (X : Polynomial k) ^ (n + 1) ∣ p := by
  rw [← RingHom.mem_ker, ker_chartHom, Ideal.mem_span_singleton]

/-- **`ε` has unbounded order of nilpotence along the charts.** The `(n + 1)`-st chart of `f` has
strictly smaller kernel than the `n`-th, so no single proper closed subscheme of `𝔸¹` contains the
scheme theoretic image of every chart. -/
theorem ker_chartHom_lt (n : ℕ) :
    RingHom.ker (chartHom k (n + 1)) < RingHom.ker (chartHom k n) := by
  rw [ker_chartHom, ker_chartHom]
  refine lt_of_le_of_ne (Ideal.span_singleton_le_span_singleton.2 ⟨X, by ring⟩) fun h => ?_
  have := (pow_dvd_pow_iff X_ne_zero not_isUnit_X).1 (Ideal.span_singleton_le_span_singleton.1 h.ge)
  omega

/-- **The only polynomial vanishing on every chart is `0`.** If `P(ε) = 0` in every `A n` then
`P = 0`: the scheme theoretic image of `f` is all of `𝔸¹`. -/
theorem eq_zero_of_forall_chartHom_eq_zero (p : Polynomial k) (h : ∀ n, chartHom k n p = 0) :
    p = 0 := by
  by_contra hne
  have hdvd := (chartHom_eq_zero_iff k p.natDegree p).1 (h p.natDegree)
  have hle := natDegree_le_of_dvd hdvd hne
  rw [natDegree_X_pow] at hle
  omega

/-- **The scheme theoretic image of `f` is all of `𝔸¹`:** the intersection of the kernels of the
charts of `f` is `0`. -/
theorem iInf_ker_chartHom : (⨅ n, RingHom.ker (chartHom k n)) = ⊥ := by
  refine le_antisymm (fun p hp => ?_) bot_le
  rw [Submodule.mem_iInf] at hp
  exact Ideal.mem_bot.2
    (eq_zero_of_forall_chartHom_eq_zero k p fun n => RingHom.mem_ker.1 (hp n))

section Dimension

theorem zeroLocus_chartIdeal (n : ℕ) :
    PrimeSpectrum.zeroLocus (chartIdeal k n : Set (Polynomial (Polynomial k))) =
      PrimeSpectrum.zeroLocus (Ideal.span {(X : Polynomial (Polynomial k))} :
        Set (Polynomial (Polynomial k))) := by
  refine Set.Subset.antisymm (fun p hp => ?_) (fun p hp => ?_)
  · rw [PrimeSpectrum.mem_zeroLocus] at hp ⊢
    refine Ideal.span_le.2 (Set.singleton_subset_iff.2 ?_)
    exact p.isPrime.mem_of_pow_mem (n + 1) (hp (X_pow_succ_mem_chartIdeal k n))
  · rw [PrimeSpectrum.mem_zeroLocus] at hp ⊢
    exact fun a ha => hp (chartIdeal_le_span_X k n ha)

/-- `k[x][ε]/(ε) ≅ k[x]`. -/
def quotientSpanXEquiv :
    (Polynomial (Polynomial k) ⧸ Ideal.span {(X : Polynomial (Polynomial k))}) ≃+*
      Polynomial k :=
  (Ideal.quotEquivOfEq (by simp :
      Ideal.span {(X : Polynomial (Polynomial k))} =
        Ideal.span {X - C (0 : Polynomial k)})).trans
    (quotientSpanXSubCAlgEquiv (0 : Polynomial k)).toRingEquiv

/-- `dim R[ε]/(ε) = dim R`. -/
private theorem ringKrullDim_quotient_span_X (R : Type*) [CommRing R] :
    ringKrullDim (R[X] ⧸ Ideal.span {(X : R[X])}) = ringKrullDim R :=
  ringKrullDim_eq_of_ringEquiv
    ((Ideal.quotEquivOfEq (by simp : Ideal.span {(X : R[X])} = Ideal.span {X - C (0 : R)})).trans
      (quotientSpanXSubCAlgEquiv (0 : R)).toRingEquiv)

theorem ringKrullDim_polynomial : ringKrullDim (Polynomial k) = 1 := by
  rw [Polynomial.ringKrullDim_of_isNoetherianRing, ringKrullDim_eq_zero_of_field, zero_add]

/-- **`dim (Spec (A n)) = 1`.** -/
theorem ringKrullDim_quotient_chartIdeal (n : ℕ) :
    ringKrullDim (Polynomial (Polynomial k) ⧸ chartIdeal k n) = 1 := by
  rw [ringKrullDim_quotient, zeroLocus_chartIdeal, ← ringKrullDim_quotient,
    ringKrullDim_quotient_span_X, ringKrullDim_polynomial]

/-- **The fibre of `f` over `t = 0` has dimension `1` on every chart.** The fibre ring is
`A n ⊗_{k[t]} k[t]/(t) = A n / (ε)`, which is `k[x]`. -/
theorem ringKrullDim_quotient_span_epsilon (n : ℕ) :
    ringKrullDim ((Polynomial (Polynomial k) ⧸ chartIdeal k n) ⧸ Ideal.span {epsilon k n}) = 1 := by
  rw [ringKrullDim_eq_of_ringEquiv (quotientSpanEpsilonEquiv k n), ringKrullDim_polynomial]

/-- **`dim 𝒵 = 1`:** the scheme theoretic image of `f` is `𝔸¹`. -/
theorem ringKrullDim_quotient_iInf_ker_chartHom :
    ringKrullDim (Polynomial k ⧸ ⨅ n, RingHom.ker (chartHom k n)) = 1 := by
  rw [ringKrullDim_eq_of_ringEquiv
    ((Ideal.quotEquivOfEq (iInf_ker_chartHom k)).trans (RingEquiv.quotientBot (Polynomial k))),
    ringKrullDim_polynomial]

/-- **The scheme theoretic image of the restriction of `f` to one chart has dimension `0`.** It is
`Spec (k[t]/(t ^ (n + 1)))`. -/
theorem ringKrullDim_quotient_ker_chartHom (n : ℕ) :
    ringKrullDim (Polynomial k ⧸ RingHom.ker (chartHom k n)) = 0 := by
  rw [ker_chartHom, ringKrullDim_quotient, PrimeSpectrum.zeroLocus_span,
    PrimeSpectrum.zeroLocus_singleton_pow _ _ n.succ_pos, ← PrimeSpectrum.zeroLocus_span,
    ← ringKrullDim_quotient, ringKrullDim_quotient_span_X, ringKrullDim_eq_zero_of_field]

/-- **The equality clause of Stacks 0DS4 fails for `f`.** On every chart of `T` the dimension of
the chart is `1` while the dimension of the scheme theoretic image `𝒵` of `f` plus the dimension
of the fibre of `f` through that chart is `1 + 1`. -/
theorem ringKrullDim_quotient_chartIdeal_ne_add (n : ℕ) :
    ringKrullDim (Polynomial (Polynomial k) ⧸ chartIdeal k n) ≠
      ringKrullDim (Polynomial k ⧸ ⨅ m, RingHom.ker (chartHom k m)) +
        ringKrullDim ((Polynomial (Polynomial k) ⧸ chartIdeal k n) ⧸
          Ideal.span {epsilon k n}) := by
  rw [ringKrullDim_quotient_chartIdeal, ringKrullDim_quotient_iInf_ker_chartHom,
    ringKrullDim_quotient_span_epsilon]
  decide

/-- **The equality is restored on a single chart, by changing `𝒵`.** With `𝒵` replaced by the
scheme theoretic image of the restriction of `f` to the quasi-compact open `Spec (A n)`, the
dimension formula holds: `1 = 0 + 1`. -/
theorem ringKrullDim_quotient_chartIdeal_eq_add_ker_chartHom (n : ℕ) :
    ringKrullDim (Polynomial (Polynomial k) ⧸ chartIdeal k n) =
      ringKrullDim (Polynomial k ⧸ RingHom.ker (chartHom k n)) +
        ringKrullDim ((Polynomial (Polynomial k) ⧸ chartIdeal k n) ⧸
          Ideal.span {epsilon k n}) := by
  rw [ringKrullDim_quotient_chartIdeal, ringKrullDim_quotient_ker_chartHom,
    ringKrullDim_quotient_span_epsilon, zero_add]

end Dimension

section Localization

/-- The inclusion `k[x] →+* A n` of the coefficient ring, `x ↦ x`. -/
def xHom (n : ℕ) : Polynomial k →+* Polynomial (Polynomial k) ⧸ chartIdeal k n :=
  (Ideal.Quotient.mk (chartIdeal k n)).comp C

@[simp]
theorem xHom_apply (n : ℕ) (p : Polynomial k) :
    xHom k n p = Ideal.Quotient.mk (chartIdeal k n) (C p) := rfl

@[simp]
theorem reduction_xHom (n : ℕ) (p : Polynomial k) : reduction k n (xHom k n p) = p := by
  rw [xHom_apply, reduction_mk, eval_C]

theorem xHom_injective (n : ℕ) : Function.Injective (xHom k n) :=
  Function.LeftInverse.injective (reduction_xHom k n)

@[simp]
theorem xHom_X (n : ℕ) : xHom k n X = xCoord k n := rfl

theorem xCoord_mul_epsilon (n : ℕ) : xCoord k n * epsilon k n = 0 := by
  rw [xCoord, epsilon, ← map_mul, Ideal.Quotient.eq_zero_iff_mem]
  exact C_X_mul_X_mem_chartIdeal k n

theorem isUnit_algebraMap_xCoord (n : ℕ) :
    IsUnit (algebraMap (Polynomial (Polynomial k) ⧸ chartIdeal k n)
      (Localization.Away (xCoord k n)) (xCoord k n)) :=
  IsLocalization.map_units (M := Submonoid.powers (xCoord k n))
    (S := Localization.Away (xCoord k n)) ⟨xCoord k n, Submonoid.mem_powers _⟩

/-- **`ε` dies in `A n [1/x]`**, because `x * ε = 0` and `x` has become invertible. -/
theorem algebraMap_epsilon_eq_zero (n : ℕ) :
    algebraMap (Polynomial (Polynomial k) ⧸ chartIdeal k n) (Localization.Away (xCoord k n))
      (epsilon k n) = 0 :=
  (isUnit_algebraMap_xCoord k n).mul_right_eq_zero.1 <| by
    rw [← map_mul, xCoord_mul_epsilon, map_zero]

theorem algebraMap_eq_algebraMap_xHom_reduction (n : ℕ)
    (a : Polynomial (Polynomial k) ⧸ chartIdeal k n) :
    algebraMap (Polynomial (Polynomial k) ⧸ chartIdeal k n) (Localization.Away (xCoord k n)) a =
      algebraMap (Polynomial (Polynomial k) ⧸ chartIdeal k n) (Localization.Away (xCoord k n))
        (xHom k n (reduction k n a)) := by
  have hmem : a - xHom k n (reduction k n a) ∈ Ideal.span {epsilon k n} := by
    rw [← ker_reduction, RingHom.mem_ker, map_sub, reduction_xHom, sub_self]
  obtain ⟨b, hb⟩ := Ideal.mem_span_singleton.1 hmem
  rw [← sub_eq_zero, ← map_sub, hb, map_mul, algebraMap_epsilon_eq_zero, zero_mul]

/-- The composite `k[x] → A n → A n [1/x]`, through which `A n [1/x]` is a `k[x]`-algebra. -/
def awayHom (n : ℕ) : Polynomial k →+* Localization.Away (xCoord k n) :=
  (algebraMap (Polynomial (Polynomial k) ⧸ chartIdeal k n)
    (Localization.Away (xCoord k n))).comp (xHom k n)

/-- **`A n [1/x] = k[x][1/x]`:** inverting `x` on the chart identifies it with the punctured
affine line, which is the open along which the charts of `T` are glued. Stated for any
`k[x]`-algebra structure on `A n [1/x]` whose structure map is the one of `AlgebraicGeometry.
ThickenedOrigin.awayHom`. -/
theorem isLocalization_away_X (n : ℕ)
    [Algebra (Polynomial k) (Localization.Away (xCoord k n))]
    (hmap : algebraMap (Polynomial k) (Localization.Away (xCoord k n)) = awayHom k n) :
    IsLocalization.Away (X : Polynomial k) (Localization.Away (xCoord k n)) := by
  refine (isLocalization_iff (Submonoid.powers (X : Polynomial k))
    (Localization.Away (xCoord k n))).2 ⟨?_, ?_, ?_⟩
  · rintro ⟨-, m, rfl⟩
    rw [hmap, awayHom, RingHom.comp_apply, map_pow, xHom_X, map_pow]
    exact (isUnit_algebraMap_xCoord k n).pow m
  · intro z
    obtain ⟨⟨a, -, m, rfl⟩, hz⟩ := IsLocalization.surj (Submonoid.powers (xCoord k n)) z
    refine ⟨⟨reduction k n a, ⟨X ^ m, m, rfl⟩⟩, ?_⟩
    rw [hmap, awayHom]
    simp only [RingHom.comp_apply, map_pow, xHom_X]
    rw [← algebraMap_eq_algebraMap_xHom_reduction, ← map_pow]
    exact hz
  · intro p q hpq
    rw [hmap, awayHom] at hpq
    simp only [RingHom.comp_apply] at hpq
    obtain ⟨⟨-, m, rfl⟩, hc⟩ :=
      IsLocalization.exists_of_eq (M := Submonoid.powers (xCoord k n)) hpq
    refine ⟨⟨X ^ m, m, rfl⟩, xHom_injective k n ?_⟩
    rw [map_mul, map_mul, map_pow, xHom_X]
    exact hc

/-- **`A n [1/x] ≅ k[x][1/x]`.** -/
def awayEquiv (n : ℕ) :
    Localization.Away (X : Polynomial k) ≃+* Localization.Away (xCoord k n) :=
  letI _inst : Algebra (Polynomial k) (Localization.Away (xCoord k n)) := (awayHom k n).toAlgebra
  haveI : IsLocalization.Away (X : Polynomial k) (Localization.Away (xCoord k n)) :=
    isLocalization_away_X k n rfl
  (IsLocalization.algEquiv (Submonoid.powers (X : Polynomial k))
      (Localization.Away (X : Polynomial k)) (Localization.Away (xCoord k n))).toRingEquiv

end Localization

section FiniteType

variable (n : ℕ) [alg : Algebra (Polynomial k) (Polynomial (Polynomial k) ⧸ chartIdeal k n)]

theorem xCoord_mem_adjoin : xCoord k n ∈ Algebra.adjoin (Polynomial k) {xCoord k n} :=
  Algebra.subset_adjoin rfl

theorem epsilon_mem_adjoin (hmap :
      algebraMap (Polynomial k) (Polynomial (Polynomial k) ⧸ chartIdeal k n) = chartHom k n) :
    epsilon k n ∈ Algebra.adjoin (Polynomial k) {xCoord k n} := by
  have h : algebraMap (Polynomial k) (Polynomial (Polynomial k) ⧸ chartIdeal k n) X =
      epsilon k n := by rw [hmap, chartHom_X]
  rw [← h]
  exact Subalgebra.algebraMap_mem _ _

theorem xHom_mem_adjoin (hmap :
      algebraMap (Polynomial k) (Polynomial (Polynomial k) ⧸ chartIdeal k n) = chartHom k n)
    (b : Polynomial k) :
    xHom k n b ∈ Algebra.adjoin (Polynomial k) {xCoord k n} := by
  induction b using Polynomial.induction_on' with
  | add u v hu hv => rw [map_add]; exact add_mem hu hv
  | monomial j c =>
    have h2 : xHom k n ((monomial j) c) =
        algebraMap (Polynomial k) (Polynomial (Polynomial k) ⧸ chartIdeal k n) (C c) *
          xCoord k n ^ j := by
      rw [hmap, chartHom_C, xCoord, ← map_pow, ← map_mul, xHom_apply,
        ← C_mul_X_pow_eq_monomial, map_mul, map_pow]
    rw [h2]
    exact mul_mem (Subalgebra.algebraMap_mem _ _) (pow_mem (xCoord_mem_adjoin k n) j)

/-- **`A n` is generated by `x` over `k[t]`,** where `k[t]` acts through `t ↦ ε`. -/
theorem adjoin_xCoord_eq_top (hmap :
      algebraMap (Polynomial k) (Polynomial (Polynomial k) ⧸ chartIdeal k n) = chartHom k n) :
    Algebra.adjoin (Polynomial k) {xCoord k n} = ⊤ := by
  refine le_antisymm le_top fun a ha => ?_
  obtain ⟨p, rfl⟩ := Ideal.Quotient.mk_surjective a
  clear ha
  induction p using Polynomial.induction_on' with
  | add p q hp hq => rw [map_add]; exact add_mem hp hq
  | monomial m b =>
    have h1 : Ideal.Quotient.mk (chartIdeal k n) ((monomial m) b) =
        xHom k n b * epsilon k n ^ m := by
      rw [xHom_apply, epsilon, ← map_pow, ← map_mul, ← C_mul_X_pow_eq_monomial, map_mul, map_pow]
    rw [h1]
    exact mul_mem (xHom_mem_adjoin k n hmap b) (pow_mem (epsilon_mem_adjoin k n hmap) m)

/-- **The chart of `f` is of finite type over `k[t]`:** `f` is locally of finite type. -/
theorem finiteType_chartHom (hmap :
      algebraMap (Polynomial k) (Polynomial (Polynomial k) ⧸ chartIdeal k n) = chartHom k n) :
    Algebra.FiniteType (Polynomial k) (Polynomial (Polynomial k) ⧸ chartIdeal k n) :=
  ⟨⟨{xCoord k n}, by simpa using adjoin_xCoord_eq_top k n hmap⟩⟩

omit alg in
/-- **The chart of `f` is of finite type over `k[t]`,** for the `k[t]`-algebra structure that the
chart itself defines. -/
theorem finiteType_toAlgebra_chartHom :
    @Algebra.FiniteType (Polynomial k) (Polynomial (Polynomial k) ⧸ chartIdeal k n) _ _
      (chartHom k n).toAlgebra :=
  finiteType_chartHom k n (alg := (chartHom k n).toAlgebra) (RingHom.algebraMap_toAlgebra _)

end FiniteType

end AlgebraicGeometry.ThickenedOrigin

